Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||11-11-2001||10:33 AM||||i know this is the fiero forum but i am trying to help a friend get his 86 sunbird 2.8 winter beater finished when i am not working on my car. one thing we cant figure out about the sunbird is the engine sounds like it has a knock when you holt it at about 2500 rpm or higher but if you let off the gas or put the pedal to the floor the knock stops until you hold the gas pedal steady at about 1/4 of the way down. i went over the entire engine with a mechanics stethoscope and it it the loudest at the fuel rail. when i put the stethoscope on the intake i could barely hear it but it was really loud on the fuel rail.  <P>could it be a bad injector knocking or not?  <BR>or what else could it be?||||reg||5
Z||000001||crypto1079||11-11-2001||11:00 AM||||I have never heard of an "injector knock". And injector is just a small electric solenoid basically.  Can't possibly imagine it making a noise loud enough to be heard over the sound of the engine.  I'd guess it's a loose valve if it's heard only up top. I'd say you need to check/adjust valve lash.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||11-11-2001||12:04 PM||||Well, 2.8 injectors make an audible clicking sound.  But that sounds more like a valve click than a knock. A loose injector?  Valve lash?  (again, that should be more of a click and a knock).  How's the oil pressure?  It could be a rod bearing about to go.  Hope not.||||reg||1
